ns have been decorating eggs for  millennia with engraved ostrich eggs  discovered in Africa going back sixty  thousand years christians of mesopotamia  stained eggs red in tribute to the blood  of christ and the egg itself represents  the resurrection of the lord but modern  adults ranked red as the least popular  color with their favorite being blue and  as always thanks for watching  you
 

